# The music player's OWN authorable components (docs/ecs-systems-own-their-
# tables.md §3): lib/ui tables until the ECS split step 4 moved them next to
# the system that reads them. A `.raescene` still authors them by name; the
# loader parks a name no lib table has in `world.pendingComponents` and
# applyMusicComponents (MusicSystems.rae) decodes each into its system.
open ui/Components

# Which live library count a `ProfileStat` node shows. Authored as the member
# name: `"ProfileStat": { "stat": "albums" }`.
enum ProfileStatKind { albums, tracks, listeningHours }

# A Text node whose `text` is a live count from the app's media library. The
# number never lives in the scene; `profileStatsSystem` writes `Text.text` on
# the same entity when the count changes (a pure data binding, no layout).
type ProfileStat {
  stat: ProfileStatKind
}

# An avatar slot whose photo may not be loaded yet. Authored on a Stack
# container with two children: the photo (the child whose `Sprite.textureKey`
# equals `textureKey`) and an authored placeholder. `avatarSystem` activates
# the photo once the texture registry holds the key and the placeholder
# otherwise, so a download that lands later is an `Active` toggle on two
# children — not a page rebuild.
type AvatarSource {
  textureKey: String
}
